      en: ["Hartford was the site of the first American school for the deaf, founded in 1817.", "The city's nickname 'Insurance Capital' dates back to the early 19th century.", "The Connecticut River is New England's longest river, at 406 miles.", "Hartford's Constitution Plaza was one of the first major urban renewal projects in the US.", "The city is the birthplace of the legendary financier J.P. Morgan.", "Hartford hosts the XL Center, a major arena for sports and concerts.", "The city has over 30 historic districts listed on the National Register of Historic Places.", "Trinity College, founded in 1823, is one of the top liberal arts colleges in the city."],
