      en: ["Augusta became the state capital in 1832, succeeding Portland.", "The city's elevation is approximately 66 feet (20 meters) above sea level.", "Augusta is the primary retail and medical hub for central Maine.", "The Kennebec River was historically used for large-scale ice harvesting.", "Charles Bulfinch, the architect of the State House, also worked on the U.S. Capitol.", "The city covers a land area of roughly 55 square miles.", "Augusta is the seat of Kennebec County, established in 1799.", "The city is located approximately 160 miles northeast of Boston."],
